.TH myst01 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
myst01, myst02, myst03, myst04, myst05, myst06, myst07, myst08, myst09,
myst10, myst11 \- Brian Howarth's Mysterious Adventures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.BR myst01 " ... " myst11
.SH DESCRIPTION
The eleven Mysterious Adventures Brian Howarth wrote between 1981 and
1983, some with Wherner Barnes or Cliff Ogden, each a program of its own
with the game built in.  These are the text-only versions.
.TP
.B myst01
The Golden Baton
.TP
.B myst02
The Time Machine
.TP
.B myst03
Arrow of Death, Part 1
.TP
.B myst04
Arrow of Death, Part 2
.TP
.B myst05
Escape from Pulsar 7
.TP
.B myst06
Circus
.TP
.B myst07
The Feasibility Experiment
.TP
.B myst08
The Wizard of Akyrz
.TP
.B myst09
Perseus and Andromeda
.TP
.B myst10
Ten Little Indians
.TP
.B myst11
Waxworks
.SH PLAYING
They play exactly as the Scott Adams games do, on the same engine: a
verb, or a verb and a noun; a single
.BR N ,
.BR S ,
.BR E ,
.BR W ,
.B U
or
.B D
to move and
.B I
for what you carry;
.B SAVE GAME
to keep a game, which each one offers to restore as it starts; and the
place you are in held at the top of the screen.
.BR adv01 (1)
has the detail.
.SH NOTES
Brian Howarth gave his permission for the games to be freely
distributed.
.SH SEE ALSO
